/-
  A `ℤ`-basis of the period lattice whose real span is everything.

  For a congruence subgroup `Γ ≤ SL(2, ℤ)` the period lattice
  `ModularCurve.periodLatticeOf Γ` is a submodule of the complex dual
  `D := Module.Dual ℂ (CuspForm Γ 2)` of the weight-two cusp forms, namely the `ℤ`-span of the
  periods `ModularCurve.periodOf Γ γ`, `γ ∈ Γ`. The headline below says that this lattice has a
  `ℤ`-basis `b : Module.Basis (Fin n) ℤ (periodLatticeOf Γ)` whose images in `D` are
  `ℝ`-linearly independent and `ℝ`-span the whole dual. Read twice, that is freeness — a `ℤ`-basis
  exists, of finite explicit rank `n` — and discreteness/cocompactness: real span top means that
  `D / periodLatticeOf Γ` is a torus. It is exactly the premise the Tate identification consumes,
  since without a free finite-rank lattice there is no `ℤ_[p] ⊗[ℤ] periodLatticeOf` to state the
  equivalence against.

  The proof (`main`) runs as follows. `SL(2, ℤ)` is generated by `S` and `T` (`fg_SL2Z`), so a
  finite-index `Γ` is finitely generated (`fg_Gamma`), and additive homomorphisms out of
  `Additive Γ` are determined by their values on a generating set
  (`addMonoidHom_eq_of_eqOn_gen`) — hence `Additive Γ →+ ℝ` is a finite `ℝ`-module
  (`finite_addMonoidHom_real`) and the `ℝ`-span `U` of the periods cannot be a proper subspace:
  a nonzero functional killing `U` would extend `ℂ`-linearly to `D` (`Module.Dual.extendRCLike`),
  be an evaluation at some `v : CuspForm Γ 2` (`Module.evalEquiv`), and the nondegeneracy
  `ModularCurve.eq_zero_of_forall_re_periodOf_eq_zero` (`PeriodLatticeRank`) would force `v = 0`.
  Separately the period map is a parabolic hom whose restriction to `Γ` is `periodOf`
  (`exists_isParabolicHom_apply_eq_periodOf`), so `periodLatticeOf Γ` is a finitely generated
  `ℤ`-module; `D` is torsion-free over `ℤ`, whence `Λ := periodLatticeOf Γ` is free. Taking
  `b := Module.finBasis ℤ Λ` and `w := Λ.subtype ∘ b`, the `ℤ`-span of `w` is `Λ`, so its
  `ℝ`-span contains every period (via `Submodule.span_le_restrictScalars`) and is `U = ⊤`; then
  `n ≤ finrank ℝ D` comes from the rank bound for congruence subgroups
  (`finrank_parabolicHoms_le_two_mul_finrank_cuspForm_of_isCongruenceSubgroup`, B4) through the
  parabolic homs `b.coord i ∘ Φ'`, and `finrank ℝ D ≤ n` from `finrank_range_le_card`, so
  `LinearIndependent ℝ w` follows from `linearIndependent_of_top_le_span_of_card_eq_finrank`.

  Transcribed from
  `P2M/Sol/S_ModularCurve_exists_basis_periodLatticeOf_linearIndependent_real_span_eq_top_of_isCongruenceSubgroup.lean`
  (pinned `aa2d8b3`, 267 lines); the statement is the `Theorems/` wrapper's. Two landed blocks are
  imported rather than transcribed: `ModularCurve.eq_zero_of_forall_re_periodOf_eq_zero`
  (`ModularCurve/Period/PeriodLatticeRank.lean`), and the whole W2 period/parabolic-homs layer
  (`exists_basis_parabolicHoms_of_isAddTorsionFree`, `periodMapOf_mem_parabolicHoms`,
  `periodMapOf_apply_eq_periodOf`) plus the general rank bound B4, all from
  `ModularCurve/Period/ParabolicHomsBasis.lean`; `CuspForm.finiteDimensional_of_isArithmetic` comes
  through with it. Every helper below is `private`, so the statement checker diffs only the
  headline.

  The pin's ~100 `attribute [-instance]` and ~200 `attribute [-simp]` entries — the largest
  instance wall in the subject — are dropped in full (D3): none of them is needed here, and no
  global attribute is reinstated.

  Following plan §5 D5 the rank number, which the pin's statement does not contain, is *derived*
  here rather than left to the consumer:
  `ModularCurve.finrank_periodLatticeOf_eq_two_mul_finrank_cuspForm` states
  `finrank ℤ (periodLatticeOf Γ) = 2 * finrank ℂ (CuspForm Γ 2)` for every congruence subgroup
  `Γ`, from the `ℝ`-linear independence plus real-span-top of the basis above. It is port-authored
  (`2 · dim_ℂ` is the dimension of the real dual), so it carries no pin name and is kept strictly
  apart from the pinned headline.

  The second row this module hosts is the perfectness of the Eichler–Shimura pairing: that the
  periods *determine* the parabolic homs, i.e. that `parabolicHoms ℤ Γ ℤ` is the `ℤ`-dual of
  `periodLatticeOf Γ` compatibly with `periodOf`. The engine (`ModularCurve.CpairK2Of` below) is
  the pin's: the periods `perΛ` span the lattice (`span_perΛ`), the `ℤ`-span of the relations
  `single (γδ) - single γ - single δ` and `single γ` for parabolic `γ` is the kernel of the period
  functional on `Γ →₀ ℤ` (`rel_le_ker_period`), so the period functional factors through the
  quotient `Q Γ` (`phiBar`); `rel_le_ker` does the same bookkeeping for an arbitrary parabolic hom,
  giving `barOf`; `dualEquiv` identifies `parabolicHoms` with `Dual (Q Γ)`; the two rank bounds
  (`exists_basis_periodLatticeOf_card_eq`, `exists_basis_parabolicHoms_card_le`) show the kernel of
  `phiBar` has zero `ℤ`-dual (`dual_ker_phiBar_eq_zero`), so a splitting of `phiBar` makes `barOf`
  injective (`main`'s `key`), and the assembly `main` produces the equivalence. Transcribed from
  `P2M/Sol/S_ModularCurve_exists_linearEquiv_parabolicHoms_dual_periodLatticeOf_apply_periodOf_of_isCongruenceSubgroup.lean`
  (pinned `aa2d8b3`, 350 lines); the statement is the `Theorems/` wrapper's. The engine is `private`
  (the wire has no statement for it); the `attribute [-instance]` / `attribute [-simp]` preludes of
